+\subsection{Robustness to Pilots, Estimation Error and Phase Resolution}
+\label{sec:res_robust}
+These checks use the aging set and the re-measured one-thread latencies (Section~\ref{sec:method}; Adam 1.33~ms per step, coordinate descent 0.70~s, long-run Adam 4.95~s). Configurations are selected on an independent mobility draw and reported with paired CIs; $L^\star$ is read on the aging set.
+
+\emph{Precoder pilots.} With the regularized zero-forcing precoder refreshed every $T_{\mathrm{r}}$~ms from four data-free pilot symbols ($T_{\mathrm{r}}$ chosen per method) and the minimum user rate averaged over $W$~ms after deployment, net of pilots ($\bar{R}_W$), the selected configuration reaches 5.21~b/s/Hz with free refresh and 3.54, 4.00 and 4.33~b/s/Hz at 15, 30 and 60~kHz ($W=50$~ms, $T_{\mathrm{r}}=1$--2~ms). Adam with 3--20 steps is tied with it (6--8 steps); coordinate descent and long-run Adam are significantly behind. For $W=25$, 50 and 100~ms the selected step counts are 5, 6--8 and 16--20 (16--24 with free refresh); at 100~ms six steps lie 0.02--0.04~b/s/Hz below.
+
+\emph{Imperfect channel knowledge.} With estimation error of power $1/(1+\rho)$ relative to the mean channel power ($\rho$: pilot signal-to-noise ratio; per-scenario median 22.6~dB at $\rho=30$~dB), the phase computed from the $t=0$ estimate and the precoder from a fresh one, the best effective rate falls from 6.08 to 3.54~b/s/Hz at 30~dB; at 10~dB and below Adam and SU-best-of are tied. With pilots charged as well ($\bar{R}_{50}$), Adam leads SU-best-of by 0.05--0.06~b/s/Hz at 30~dB and ties it at 20~dB; coordinate descent and long-run Adam stay significantly behind.
+
+\emph{Discrete phases.} Rounding the phases of Adam (step size 0.5) and SU-best-of to $2^b$ levels at no time cost keeps an intrinsic optimum ($L^\star=5$, 6, 6 for $b=1$, 2, 3; $L=48$ costs 9.5, 14.1, 14.9\%). Discrete coordinate descent on the $2^b$ levels (16--501~ms) is significantly behind rounded SU-best-of at $b=3$, and at $b=2$ with two or more sweeps. At $b=1$ it is selected with a single sweep (16~ms): 0.25~b/s/Hz (CI 0.16--0.33) above rounded SU-best-of and tied with the best rounded Adam ($-0.04$, CI $-0.11$ to 0.02).
